description: Required shared design context and review gates for this site
alwaysApply: true
---

Read AGENTS.md and the current approved brief before changing the site.
Run `npm run verify:design` in the site folder before implementation.
Stop if any file is missing or its hash differs. Restore the approved full library; never replace it with a summary.
Follow `.agents/skills/studio-design-gate/SKILL.md`. Design skill precedence: YC Interface Craft leads visual direction (its SKILL.md plus only the 3-5 matching research records); Intentional UI Design sets the quality floor; frontend-design guides composition and type. Illustration, motion and component skills load only when the design contract names them.
Record the paths actually read in `evidence/design-skills-read.md`. A hash check alone is not a load acknowledgment.
This starter has no page design. Replace the placeholder page with components written for `design/contract.md`. Never build a data-driven section builder.
Build only the hero and first proof section first. Capture 1440px and 390px screenshots in Cloud. Build nothing else until the Designer and the marketing reviewer both PASS Gate 1 in `design/gate.json`.
Do not restart design exploration after a choice. Do not invent proof, prices, people or customer logos.
Gate 2 reviews the full rendered desktop and phone site before the owner review. Also check the keyboard path, errors, useful result and reduced motion.
Return actual source, logs, screenshots, run URL and model evidence to the PM. Stop before deployment.


## Current handoff

Before launch and after each feedback or scope change, get the current PM brief and approved design/copy handoff. Record their versions, approval state and file hashes in a handoff manifest. Send updated files to the same Cloud run and require acknowledgment of the received versions before further implementation. Recover existing approvals from PM; do not ask the owner to repeat them. An initial upload does not carry later decisions. Distinguish an uploaded archive audit from verification of files inside the live Cloud workspace.
